  "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves an operational problem where canonical CI's `build-artifacts` job spends roughly three minutes rebuilding TypeScript during the built Doctor plugin-index persistence proof, even though the job created the exact `dist/` artifact immediately beforehand.\n\nAcross the latest 12 successful main runs sampled before this change, `build-artifacts` took 349–462 seconds and the Doctor proof alone took 186–262 seconds. In the first warm post-optimization main run, that step consumed 188 of the job's 351 seconds while its test body took about 8 seconds.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe built Doctor proof now sets the E2E harness's existing `OPENCLAW_E2E_USE_PREBUILT_DIST=1` contract, matching the exact-artifact SQLite proof already in the workflow. This preserves the same built-CLI test while skipping only the E2E global setup's fallback TypeScript build. The existing workflow guard now locks that contract, and the CI documentation records the ownership boundary.\n\nThis does not add fanout, change runner classes, reduce coverage, alter dependencies, or route canonical CI through Crabbox.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDevelopers should receive `build-artifacts` results roughly 2.5–4 minutes sooner when it is on the CI critical path, with no reduction in validation coverage. Based on the sampled runs, the job's median runtime should fall from roughly 380 seconds toward 180–190 seconds.\n\n## Evidence\n\nAI-assisted maintainer change; the author understands and reviewed the workflow behavior.\n\nMeasured before:\n\n- Main run 31568650453, job 94026523319: `build-artifacts` 351s; Doctor proof 188s; test body 8.09s.\n- Main run 31567558183, job 94024246098: `build-artifacts` 433s; Doctor proof 189s.\n- Latest 12 successful main runs sampled: job 349–462s; Doctor proof 186–262s, median about 198s.\n- The Doctor logs report the duplicate build trigger: `dist is stale: missing_private_qa_dist`.\n\nFocused local proof on Node 24.19.0:\n\n- YAML contract probe: base `false`, patched `true`.\n- Workflow YAML parse: pass.\n- `oxfmt --check .github/workflows/ci.yml docs/ci.md test/scripts/ci-workflow-guards.test.ts`: pass.\n- `node scripts/docs-list.js`: pass.\n- `git diff --check`: pass.\n- Autoreview TruffleHog scan: clean. The model review phase was unavailable in the orb because no authenticated reviewer CLI was available.\n\nExact-head hosted CI and a manual full CI run will provide executable workflow proof before landing.\n",
